_dev\loop-engineering\runtime\logs\20260804_175718_step_3-4.log:14079:Capture/generate and validate the fixture inventory defined in 0.2 before building the UI; fixtures must be deterministic, sanitized, small, and independent of live providers. Add `stub.input` (Sample Input) and `stub.output` (Result Viewer) to the registry with dynamic `port_type` resolution in the compatibility matrix. Frontend: dropping a node with no connections auto-spawns one pre-connected Sample Input stub per required input and one Result Viewer on the principal output; half-height dashed rendering with "sample" badge; connecting a real edge to a stubbed input removes that stub (undoably); auto-attach toggle in workflow settings; manual attach via library "Testing" category and node context menu. Stub payloads editable in the inspector with per-port-type validation; file-backed types reference bundled fixtures only (never browser-supplied paths).
